// Words one tongue borrowed from another instead of inheriting them from the
// First Speech. Read by src/names/mod.rs. A borrowed word starts from the
// lender's finished word and is fitted to the borrower's sounds (the
// `..._borrows` list in sounds.ron).
//
// Ṭaḍoro borrows the most: the Air-kind found no towns and lodge in other
// peoples' homes, so the words for what their hosts make and keep are their
// hosts' words.
//
//   root   the root's English key (roots.ron)
//   into   the tongue that borrowed it
//   from   the tongue it was borrowed from
//   why    the reason
[
    (root: "mountain", into: Tadoro, from: Roduro, why: "The Roduro hold the hills; wanderers learned the mountains' names from them."),
    (root: "rock", into: Tadoro, from: Roduro, why: "Stone is Roduro business."),
    (root: "town", into: Tadoro, from: Roduro, why: "The Air-kind found no towns of their own."),
    (root: "law", into: Tadoro, from: Roduro, why: "A lodger lives under the host's law."),
    (root: "tradition", into: Tadoro, from: Roduro, why: "Goes with law."),
    (root: "iron", into: Tadoro, from: Qotiro, why: "Iron is bought from Qotiro forges."),
    (root: "fight", into: Tadoro, from: Qotiro, why: "The word of the duelling yards."),
]
